# Buildroot requires this file to exist in a br2-external tree, even when the
# tree adds no packages of its own. Rivet adds none: `ADR-009` §6 draws the
# boundary at "Buildroot produces a bag of correctly-built binaries and a
# toolchain; it does not decide what the filesystem looks like". A Rivet
# package here would be Rivet's build logic living inside Buildroot, which is
# the failure that ADR's "against" column named.
#
# What this tree carries instead is a defconfig and two kernel fragments —
# configuration, not code.
